{"t": 44.104, "n": 56, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I emptied the Completed cell of every task row in `docs/plans/i153.plan.md`. The status is still `planned`. I changed nothing else, and I ran nothing, since this step has no shell.\n\n- **Marks:** The gate flagged rows 1.1 to 3.2 because their files changed after the marking commit. Row 1.3 also differed from its marked version. It also listed rows 3.3, 3.4 and 4.13 as unopened, so I treated them as unkept too. I couldn't check the marking commits without git. Rows 3.5 to 5.2 weren't flagged, but I cleared them as well, which means the code step will rebuild them. An empty mark is never refused.\n- **Files opened:** I read each file the rows name before this edit:\n  - `tests/test_usage_limit.py`, `test_workflow_packages.py`\n  - `run/nodes.py` (the `_session`, `step`, `judge` and `gate` sections), `council_run.py`, `gate.py`, `runner.py`\n  - `model/flow.py`, `durability/status.py`, `observe/detail.py`\n  - the three `diagram/model.json` files, the guide and `pauses.md`\n- **Rows and proof table:** I left the row text as it was. Every requirement has a row, and each test row comes before the code rows it covers. Both docs under Docs to update (`running-workflows.guide.md`, `pauses.md`) have a docs row. AC 1 to AC 8 each have a proof row naming `tests/test_usage_limit.py` and the command that runs it.\n- **Commands:** All four verification commands start with `cd plugins/tempergraph/engine &&` and then `python -m pytest`, `ruff check` or `mypy`. Those three are declared in the root `tempergraph.commands.json`. The two `python -m pytest` commands are the only ones that run the new tests.\n- **Not checked:** I didn't check whether the base-branch spec change from the reason for this visit affects the plan's requirements. The suite failures the last attempt reported (including `up.py::test_a_clean_finished_run_is_removed_and_its_branch_stays`) are a code-step matter. Nothing in this plan's phases touches `up.py`.\n\nARTIFACT phases: docs/plans/i153.plan.md", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "1b367713-46ed-4de8-833b-b9fbaeca31a5"}
